      "title": "rawshark: Fix rlim_t handling on Big Endian platforms",
      "message": "rawshark: Fix rlim_t handling on Big Endian platforms\n\nPOSIX says[1]:\n\nThe <sys/resource.h> header shall define the following type through typedef:\n\nrlim_t\n    Unsigned integer type used for limit values.\n\nThat does not say anything about the size. On many 32-bit platforms,\nrlim_t as defined in <sys/resource.h> is 64-bit (in order to provide\nlarge file support, etc.) although it can be handled in a fairly\ncomplicated way at the syscall level (or even accepted and made\nunlimited on sufficiently early versions of glibc.)\n\nHandle both 32 and 64 bit rlim_t, in a way that doesn't cause problems\non Big Endian platforms.\n\nCoverity CID 1646778 & 1646779\n\n[1] https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9799919799/basedefs/sys_resource.h.html\n\nFixup 7b048f64a9273c3ce141ce5e41ff4aa8db00999a\n",
